I think I'm removing any and all reference to HTML5
:)
on that note, I think I'll reintroduce set/getPreference again
Re section 1. - Marcos agreed to provide test for the Introduction, right?
Re Section 1.1 - I would remove the following sentence until the document actually exists:&quot;The Widgets 1.0: Security Model [Widgets-Security] specification defines a security model that defines what a widget can or cannot do at runtime.&quot;
4dd217ba7542bb00a127f682e2c3ad27: For the introduction, I'm basically thinking lifting most of the widget one
