CONVERSATION:
Hey.
Hello
How&apos;s it going?
Haha, I was about to type the same thing.
Not too badly; how about you?
lol I beat you to the punch, sorry.
I&apos;m pretty good, thank you. What&apos;s your name?
Stranger.
Omegle does not lie.
lol Seriously.
It&apos;s Svetlana.
Hello?
Hello Svetlana. I&apos;m Rob. Nice to meet you.
Tell me a litle bit more about yourself....
It&apos;s nice for me to meet you as well.
Um... you&apos;re not looking for a date, are you?
Because Omegle is not a great place to meet people, Rob.
lol No. It&apos;s be kind of hard to go on a date over the internet.
Where would we go, an internet cafe? lol
Of course.
Sip our e-mochas...
lol
I&apos;m just bored...and looking to chat. I like to chat with different people.
Okay, now that I&apos;m satisfied that you&apos;re not a pervert who&apos;s going to use my IP address to track me down.
Yeah, you get all types over the Internet.
Which is not always a good thing.
Yes you do...by the way....what&apos;s your address and how fast can you send me nude pictures???? (lol just kidding) =P
I&apos;m pretty normal, I guess....well what&apos;s normal anyway?
I ask myself that question every day.
Sooooo are you going to tell me more about yourself now?
If everyone is unique, is the &quot;norm&quot; to be different?
I say that all the TIME!
Woah. Serendipity.
Everyone is trying to be unique, which makes being normal actually unique
lol
But what is normal?
If normal is different, is there a real normal?
If you&apos;re being unique, does that make you normal? And does that make you unique?
The definition of normal is like trying to figure out how many licks it takes to get to the center of a tootsie pop.....the world may never know! lol
Haha, except I think that question is pretty easy to find out.
I mean, if you have a Tootsie Pop.
ah-1, ah-2, ah-3- CRUNCH! ah-3
And if you have a clear definition of &quot;center&quot;.
And if you know how to count.
lol
Haha, right.
yes but not everyone licks with the power...which gives people a varied answer
with the SAME* power
Well, that&apos;s the human factor.
Not everyone gets the same result with each experiment.
There has to be a variable.
Also, the Tootsie Pops would have to be regulated.
They&apos;d have to come from the same batch, formed the same way...
Therefore not everyone gets the same result when they &quot;attempt&quot; to be normal or unique
Same goes for people.
But how do you classify those?
What IS normal?
50%?
45%
83%?
What is unique?
Everyone is different.
But if we&apos;re different in that we&apos;re different, are we truly different?
This is getting pretty philosophical here, Rob.
This is the type of convo where pot is needed...lol we need pot and Plato here with us
Socrates too
maybe Aristotle can join in
Hey, don&apos;t forget Aristotle.
And Isaac Newton.
lol Great minds think alike, dont they?
Haha, of course.
Except not always.
Why stop there, howabout Albert Einstein and Steven Hawkins.....lets leave out Frued....he&apos;s nut
See Aristotle v. Plato.
He&apos;d tell us that we&apos;re all sexually frustrated and recommend we have instant group sex
...actually, that sounds like a GREAT IDEA!
lol
just kidding
Over the Internet, Rob?"")
