Listening on LPF/eth0/00:80:ad:70:72:b7
Sending on   LPF/eth0/00:80:ad:70:72:b7
Sending on   Socket/fallback/fallback-net
DHCPREQUEST on eth0 to 255.255.255.255 port 67
DHCPACK from 213.66.208.1
bound to 213.66.208.65 -- renewal in 600 seconds.
ok, so you get a dhcprequest and dhcpack
what if you do an ifdown and ifup and then a dhclient?
ifdown eth0 just says not configurated, ifup will probably do nothing.
dhclient will give dhrequest
its the other way round
if eth0 is configured ifup will do nothing
if its not configured it will try to configure itself
well, it saids its not configurated, but cant configure it
release the address and then redo the dhclient
dhclient -r
aha, is that release?
so I do dhclient -r eth0;ifup -a
how do I release an ip in linux? I mean like ipconfig /release in windows
dhclient -r
okey, I'll try that then
don't work. It wont take the -r argument
Usage: dhclient [-c] [-d] [-e] [-p &lt;port&gt;] [-lf lease-file]
[-pf pidfile] [interface]
oh crap what Im getting tired of this...
the old dhclient may not have the -r option
weird
try ifconfig eth0 down
and then ifup
(I will lose the internetconnection when I do ifconfig down)
yes
okey, see you in a few minutes
Still here?
starfishy: could it matter that when I first installed debian it used eth1 as external IF, and when I rebooted it changed to eth0?
Cause I think my isp lockes on MAC-address for 20 lease time
but then the dhclient wouldnt work either
or, the MAC-address are still the same
cause its just the description that have change
d
i had the same problem a couple of times that different kernels would probe the interfaces in different order
if its the same interface the mac address is the same
yes, I haven't switched any cables
ok, then its not the MAC address
nope
the configuration in /etc/network/interfaces is ok also
so ...
back to square one
:)
comment the eth0 statement in /etc/network/interfaces out
so the interface wont come up on reboot
reboot
capture the sequence from manual ifup eth0
reboot
capture the sequence from dhclient
compare the twain
shall I remove eht0 from auto-line too?
yeah
actually you need the iface line
so just remove the auto eth0
okey, so remove auto, reboot, ifup eth0, copy, save, reboot, dhclient eth0, copy, save, compare
I'll be back in a while
starfishy: Hi!
well, same as before
