85f8845005af166948e6b56e31d343c5: Depends which old doctypes you mean
Well, I'm working on switching Wikipedia from XHTML 1.0 Transitional to HTML 5.
When I switch the doctype, rendering breaks.
That will make things *much* more complicated.
I had thought that the doctype was chosen specifically so it would trigger standards mode in all browsers, but it seems that's not quite the case.
Hmm.
85f8845005af166948e6b56e31d343c5: If I'm reading the table on http://hsivonen.iki.fi/doctype/ properly, XHTML 1.0 Transitional is &quot;Almost Standards&quot;
Yeah, I just read that too.
(and &lt;!doctype html&gt; is &quot;Standards&quot;)
Okay, I'm going to have to come up with a test case here.
Because I'm seeing the rendering break in Chrome.
I'll figure out what's going on.
Hopefully there shouldn't be that many differences between almost-standards and standards
doesn't remember exactly what the differences are, though
Oh, I see.
Hmm.
Oh, http://hsivonen.iki.fi/doctype/ already talks about Almost Standards
Current MediaWiki doctype: &lt;!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC &quot;-//W3C//DTD XHTML 1.0 Transitional//EN&quot; &quot;http://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/DTD/xhtml1-transitional.dtd&quot;&gt;
