here /usr/share/tomcat-5.5/server/lib
if I symlink my package root here then my jsp compiles fine
hmm.  That's bad.
so I am thinking I need to configure my classpath for the webapp
You shouldn't need to.. and you shouldn't do it that way.
The classes you're symlinking into /usr/share/tomcat-5.5/server/lib, are they all also in &lt;my webapp&gt;/WEB-INF/classes/&lt;packageroot&gt;?
ok what should I do
yeah
Are they jar files?  Or, are they loose .class files?
the actual path is /home/http/jsp/
loose class files
Are the class files declared in a package?
What do you mean /home/http/jsp?  What is that path?  Is that what &lt;my webapp&gt; is, as shown in the path &lt;my webapp&gt;/WEB-INF/classes/&lt;packageroot&gt;?
yes
(first question) there is the a package def in the class file but there is no package description file
I am new to packaging classes
untill recently I have only developed in basic and php
Okay, so .. you put &quot;package something;&quot; in your source.. when you place the .class file in WEB-INF/classes, did you create a dir called &quot;something&quot;, and place the .class file inside it?
